WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.339
Segmentation, targeting and positioning.

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:05.096
Split the market into groups,

00:00:05.146 --> 00:00:06.594
choose which ones to serve,

00:00:06.644 --> 00:00:09.322
then own a distinct place in their minds.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.363
Picture the plaza.

00:00:11.413 --> 00:00:15.844
Students want cheap and quick, parents want healthy, and seniors want a chat.

00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:17.943
Each group is a segment.

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:21.283
Targeting means choosing, with trade-offs.

00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:23.359
Apple picked people who value premium tech and simplicity,

00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:27.743
and positioned itself on unlocking their creativity.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:29.539
Use it like this:

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:30.694
for any brand,

00:00:30.744 --> 00:00:32.204
name the segment you'd target,

00:00:32.254 --> 00:00:33.054
why,

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:35.399
and the single position you'd own.
